$$\begin{align*}
|\mathbf{a}| &= \sqrt{4^2 + 1^2} \\
&= \sqrt{17} \\
\hat{\mathbf{a}} &= \frac{\mathbf{a}}{|\mathbf{a}|} \\
&= \frac{4}{\sqrt{17}}\mathbf{i} + \frac{1}{\sqrt{17}}\mathbf{j}
\end{align*}$$

For $|\mathbf{p}+\mathbf{q}|$ to be a minimum, $\mathbf{q}$ is in the opposite direction to $\mathbf{p}$.
$$\begin{align*}
\mathbf{q}&=-20\left(\frac{1}{17}\begin{pmatrix}15 \\ -8\end{pmatrix}\right) \\
&=\begin{pmatrix}-\frac{300}{17} \\ \frac{160}{17}\end{pmatrix}
\end{align*}$$
Therefore:
$$\begin{align*}
\mathbf{a}&=\mathbf{p}+\mathbf{q} \\
&=\begin{pmatrix}15 \\ -8\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}-\frac{300}{17} \\ \frac{160}{17}\end{pmatrix} \\
&=\begin{pmatrix}-\frac{45}{17} \\ \frac{24}{17}\end{pmatrix}
\end{align*}$$

Since $\mathbf{b}$ is perpendicular to $\mathbf{p}=\begin{pmatrix}15 \\ -8\end{pmatrix}$ and has positive components, it has direction $\begin{pmatrix}8 \\ 15\end{pmatrix}$.
Let $\mathbf{b}=k\begin{pmatrix}8 \\ 15\end{pmatrix}$.
$$\begin{align*}
|\mathbf{b}|&=20 \\
\left|k\begin{pmatrix}8 \\ 15\end{pmatrix}\right|&=20 \\
17k&=20 \\
k&=\frac{20}{17}
\end{align*}$$
Hence:
$$\begin{align*}
\mathbf{b}&=\frac{20}{17}\begin{pmatrix}8 \\ 15\end{pmatrix} \\
&=\begin{pmatrix}\frac{160}{17} \\ \frac{300}{17}\end{pmatrix}
\end{align*}$$

